# How to cite PhysKit. The author list matches the paper's. GitHub shows this file as "Cite this
# repository"; Zenodo reads it when it archives a release. The version is deliberately absent: each
# tagged release is the version, and its Zenodo DOI pins it. Add the arXiv identifier to
# preferred-citation once the preprint is posted.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use PhysKit, please cite the paper below, and the software version you used (each release has
  its own DOI on Zenodo).
type: software
title: "PhysKit: agent skills for rigorous research in the physical sciences"
authors:
